# Module 3 — Consuming APIs in JavaScript
# Try each request here before writing the JavaScript that sends it.
# GitHub is still facilitator-only (60 requests per hour for the whole lab).

@openmeteo = https://api.open-meteo.com/v1
@jsonph = https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com
@httpbin = https://httpbin.org

# =====================================================================
# Lab — the weather widget
# =====================================================================

### W1. Current weather, Bengaluru (the widget's request) — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — "current": {time, temperature_2m, relative_humidity_2m, weather_code, wind_speed_10m, apparent_temperature}
# INSPECT: access-control-allow-origin: *  (a browser may call this API)
GET {{openmeteo}}/forecast?latitude=12.97&longitude=77.59&current=temperature_2m,relative_humidity_2m,weather_code,wind_speed_10m,apparent_temperature&timezone=Asia/Kolkata

### W2. A variable that doesn't exist — expect 400
# Status: 400 Bad Request — {"error": true, "reason": "..."}: Open-Meteo says why in the body
GET {{openmeteo}}/forecast?latitude=12.97&longitude=77.59&current=temprature_2m

# =====================================================================
# Exercise 3 — pagination
# =====================================================================

### P1. Page 1 of the posts, 10 per page — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — ids 1–10; X-Total-Count: 100
GET {{jsonph}}/posts?_page=1&_limit=10

### P2. Page 2 — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — ids 11–20; X-Total-Count: 100
# INSPECT: Access-Control-Expose-Headers: X-Total-Count (so browser code can read it)
GET {{jsonph}}/posts?_page=2&_limit=10

### P3. The last page — expect 200
# Status: 200 OK — ids 91–100
GET {{jsonph}}/posts?_page=10&_limit=10

### P4. Past the end — expect 200 with an empty array
# Status: 200 OK — []: an empty answer, not an error
GET {{jsonph}}/posts?_page=11&_limit=10

# =====================================================================
# getResponse's three checks (slides 5–7)
# =====================================================================

### H1. Slow: 5 seconds — expect 200 after 5 s (the page uses an 8 s limit)
# Status: 200 OK after ~5 s
GET {{httpbin}}/delay/5

### H2. A status failure — expect 404
# Status: 404 NOT FOUND — reason "http", status 404
GET {{httpbin}}/status/404

### H3. Not JSON — expect 200 with Content-Type text/html
# Status: 200 OK — Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8 → reason "format"
GET {{httpbin}}/html

### H4. A rate limit with Retry-After — expect 429
# Status: 429 TOO MANY REQUESTS — (httpbin sends no Retry-After; real APIs often do)
GET {{httpbin}}/status/429
